Key Architectural Decisions
Dual-Risk Approach: Separates environmental/temporal factors (ML model) from structural factors (geometry analysis) for more robust predictions.

Real-Time Weather Integration: Uses live weather data instead of historical averages for responsive risk assessment.

Transfer Learning: Trains on US accident data but applies to Chennai roads, assuming similar causal relationships.

Caching Strategy: Frontend caches predictions to minimize API calls and improve user experience.

Geospatial Grounding: Geometry features prevent bias toward high-traffic routes; curves and intersections are inherently riskier.

Explainability Focus: Rules-based explanation system provides immediate, understandable insights without computational overhead.

Microservices Architecture: Separate Python ML engine allows for independent scaling and technology choices.

This platform demonstrates a production-ready approach to geospatial risk assessment, combining machine learning with domain expertise in transportation safety.

